61dab5c89190b16a6997","event_uuid":"633253e2-d8f1-4a17-be4c-ff4f00efb959","position":{"commit_sha":"e7a9b9d30d0b2b19c0455cb6de2563ac943d7685","position":"1788835647259220001-633253e2-d8f1-4a17-be4c-ff4f00efb959"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Execution-plan correction: the immutable 0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e comparison failed only for _cloud_mutation_support.py because merged commit 88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684 changed its executable engine-path imports after that base. The current leaf base 665d1d0480187380f82e59bd95af1f0c44274732 contains that refactor and has the same three target blobs as the prior signed-review snapshot 12a10f3ab4effc1fbad58f47c1dab80e34f07744. Corrected the description and immutable AST command to 665d1d; also aligned local verification with the operator's documentation-only policy (focused checks plus lint/typecheck, full suite in Gerrit CI). A fresh plan review is required before implementation resumes.","timestamp":1788834366387188001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Corrected execution plan passed refreshed plan review at immutable leaf base 665d1d0480187380f82e59bd95af1f0c44274732. Signed PASS, material ccd00447bab19766, blocking findings 0. Deferred the minor P6 advisory because the seven first-class DD entries already separate the executable checks, the live nodes are collection-only rather than operational evidence, and another description edit would invalidate the current signature without changing scope.","timestamp":1788835198384019001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Local documentation commit 5e6f49b6ca3cc59085614db2f2f1b8b22c0c1027 is ready for independent TSV review. Evidence: refreshed signed plan PASS at 665d1d; immutable normalized-AST/runtime/directive/shebang guard PASS; exact HEAD^..HEAD path set PASS; 5 hermetic workflow tests PASS; 2 live lifecycle nodes collected without execution; comment hygiene PASS; diff integrity PASS; make lint PASS; make typecheck PASS; commit-ticket verifier PASS; DCO and Change-Id present. Word counts are 180->53, 80->52, and 191->72. No push or close attempted. Gerrit remains blocked by deserved-rubidium-pussycat, and this leaf still requires a reviewer-authored TSV.","timestamp":1788835647259220001}],"created_at":1788571007808833079,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"885d9da9-0444-4988-9ae8-052fc66b934f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1ff6-6c78-a91e-43c1"},{"link_uuid":"df65fa26-535a-4688-b2b6-4e925a82af9f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1580-f6c2-7f9d-4267"},{"link_uuid":"31339e9b-cbac-47ab-85f5-3fa1e60a923e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"13cb-dbdf-44cd-4661"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThree `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation` files contain three audited module-docstring blocks. Their blobs and contracts were revalidated against immutable leaf base `665d1d0480187380f82e59bd95af1f0c44274732`. This base includes the canonical reconciler-engine import-path refactor in `_cloud_mutation_support.py`; the documentation edit must preserve that executable state.\n\n## Approach and identity\nCondense only allowlisted ordinary comments and true leading docstrings. Preserve all runtime strings, prompts, fixtures, decorators, assertions, subprocess arguments, and executable behavior. Stable block IDs are `path::module-docstring`, `path::<qualified-symbol>-docstring`, or `path::<qualified-symbol>::comment(<opening words>)`; use `<module>` as the owner for module-level comments. The line spans below are immutable base citations, never the identity anchor. Adjacent blank-line cleanup is allowed only when attached to an edited block.\n\nFor each declared path, compare the immutable `665d1d0480187380f82e59bd95af1f0c44274732:<path>` blob directly with the final leaf commit, even if the implementation branch is based on a later main. Parse with `type_comments=True`; remove only allowlisted leading docstrings from `ast.Module`, `ast.ClassDef`, `ast.FunctionDef`, and `ast.AsyncFunctionDef` by their qualified-owner anchors; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; and require the remaining AST to match. This preserves runtime strings and every executable expression. Tokenize comments and compare every matched directive-bearing physical line plus any shebang byte-for-byte. The exact leaf changed-path set (`HEAD^..HEAD`) must equal the first-class `file_impact` set.\n\n## Scope — immutable base citations\n- `_cloud_mutation_support.py:1-21` — preserve bounded blast radius, run-unique labels, primary deletion, and sweep backstops.\n- `conftest.py:1-9` — preserve explicit canary enrollment, client ownership, and cleanup role.\n- `test_cloud_coordinator_lifecycle.py:1-20` — preserve the public-facade boundary, one-plan scope, live-write safety, and teardown guarantees.\n\nConsumers are pytest fixture discovery; the lifecycle module imports the support helper; `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml` and the directory README invoke the live suite; and `tests/unit/test_external_integration_cloud_mutation_workflow.py` pins the workflow lane. No target-specific runtime docstring reader was found. Preserve `_cloud_mutation_support.py` `noqa: BLE001` directives at pinned lines 145/154 and lifecycle `noqa: E402` directives at 35-38/43 byte-for-byte; preserve exact shebang absence.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes exactly the declared `file_impact` paths and only allowlisted prose blocks or their adjacent blank lines; the immutable-base normalized-AST/runtime/directive/shebang guard passes.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and retains its listed contract and real consumers; repetition, chronology, obvious narration, and ornament are removed rather than moved.\n- [ ] A reviewer who did not author the edits posts a leaf-linked TSV with one row per edited block: stable block ID, immutable-before citation, final-commit citation (or `DELETED` plus surviving neighbor), preserved contract/consumer, `directives_exact`, before/after words, reviewer session, `semantic-preservation`, and `bloat-removal`.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `directives_exact=PASS`, `semantic-preservation=PASS`, and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing rows, duplicate IDs, bad citations, or any non-PASS result block closure.\n- [ ] The focused hermetic checks, `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv lint/typecheck checks all pass. Collection-only checks never execute live Jira mutations; the full suite is delegated to Gerrit CI for this documentation-only leaf.\n\n## Verification\nThe authoritative executable commands and DD intent are recorded in first-class `verify_commands`. Run the scoped lint/typecheck and focused checks locally; Gerrit CI owns full-suite verification for this documentation-only leaf.\n\nLive Jira tests are collection-only here. The five offline workflow nodes execute normally; neither live lifecycle node may execute as part of this ticket's focused verification.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/_cloud_mutation_support.py","reason":"Condense the support module docstring while preserving bounded mutation, unique labels, deletion, and sweep backstops."},{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/conftest.py","reason":"Condense the fixture module docstring while preserving canary enrollment, client ownership, and cleanup."},{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/test_cloud_coordinator_lifecycle.py","reason":"Condense the lifecycle module docstring while preserving public-facade, one-plan, live-write, and teardown guarantees."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","2d43-3c39-307e-4450"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2d43-3c39-307e-4450","parent_status_uuid":"148e76ea-5f09-4a6c-8be0-ffd97907f457","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"e9de-5f68-6a83-42e1","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation","verify_commands":[{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c 'import ast,io,re,subprocess,sys,tokenize\nBASE=\"665d1d0480187380f82e59bd95af1f0c44274732\"\nALLOWED={\"tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/_cloud_mutation_support.py\":[\"<module>\"],\"tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/conftest.py\":[\"<module>\"],\"tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/test_cloud_coordinator_lifecycle.py\":[\"<module>\"]}\nPAT=re.compile(r\"#\\s*(?:noqa\\b|type:\\s*ignore\\b|pragma:\\s*no cover\\b|pyright:|mypy:|ruff:|pylint:|(?:fmt|isort):\\s*(?:on|off|skip)\\b|nosec\\b|coding[:=]|[A-Za-z][\\w-]*(?:-ok|-via):)\",re.I)\nclass Strip(ast.NodeTransformer):\n def __init__(self,allowed): self.allowed=allowed;self.stack=[]\n def enter(self,node,q):\n  self.stack.append(q)\n  if q in self.allowed and node.body and isinstance(node.body[0],ast.Expr) and isinstance(node.body[0].value,ast.Constant) and isinstance(node.body[0].value.value,str): node.body.pop(0)\n  node=self.generic_visit(node);self.stack.pop();return node\n def visit_Module(self,node): return self.enter(node,\"<module>\")\n def named(self,node):\n  parent=self.stack[-1] if self.stack else \"<module>\";q=node.name if parent==\"<module>\" else parent+\".\"+node.name;return self.enter(node,q)\n def visit_ClassDef(self,node): return self.named(node)\n def visit_FunctionDef(self,node): return self.named(node)\n def visit_AsyncFunctionDef(self,node): return self.named(node)\ndef src(ref,path): return subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"show\",f\"{ref}:{path}\"],text=True)\ndef norm(text,path):\n tree=Strip(set(ALLOWED.get(path,[]))).visit(ast.parse(text,filename=path,type_comments=True))\n for node in ast.walk(tree):\n  if isinstance(node,ast.TypeIgnore): node.lineno=0\n return ast.dump(tree,annotate_fields=True,include_attributes=False)\ndef protected(text):\n lines=text.splitlines()\n chosen=[lines[t.start[0]-1] for t in tokenize.generate_tokens(io.StringIO(text).readline) if t.type==tokenize.COMMENT and PAT.search(t.string)]\n return (lines[0] if lines and lines[0].startswith(\"#!\") else \"\"),chosen\nbad_ast=[];bad_protected=[]\nfor path in sys.argv[1:]:\n before=src(BASE,path);after=src(\"HEAD\",path)\n if norm(before,path)!=norm(after,path): bad_ast.append(path)\n if protected(before)!=protected(after): bad_protected.append(path)\nassert not bad_ast,f\"non-allowlisted-docstring or executable AST/runtime changes: {bad_ast}\"\nassert not bad_protected,f\"directive/shebang changes: {bad_protected}\"' tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/_cloud_mutation_support.py tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/conftest.py tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/test_cloud_coordinator_lifecycle.py","dd_id":"immutable-prose-only","dd_text":"Compare 665d1d0480187380f82e59bd95af1f0c44274732 target blobs with the final commit; strip only allowlisted qualified-owner docstrings and preserve all other docstrings, executable AST/runtime strings, and exact directive/shebang lines."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c 'import subprocess,sys\nactual=sorted(subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"diff\",\"--name-only\",\"HEAD^\",\"HEAD\"],text=True).splitlines())\nexpected=sorted(sys.argv[1:])\nassert actual==expected,f\"changed paths differ: actual={actual}, expected={expected}\"' tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/_cloud_mutation_support.py tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/conftest.py tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/test_cloud_coordinator_lifecycle.py","dd_id":"exact-leaf-paths","dd_text":"Require the leaf commit changed-path set to equal the declared file-impact set exactly."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py","dd_id":"comment-hygiene","dd_text":"Run the repository-supported narrow comment-hygiene signal."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q tests/unit/test_external_integration_cloud_mutation_workflow.py::test_workflow_is_dispatchable_and_scheduled tests/unit/test_external_integration_cloud_mutation_workflow.py::test_lane_exports_the_run_scoped_teardown_label tests/unit/test_external_integration_cloud_mutation_workflow.py::test_lane_runs_check_access_preflight_then_the_live_module tests/unit/test_external_integration_cloud_mutation_workflow.py::test_lane_wires_the_existing_cloud_credentials tests/unit/test_external_integration_cloud_mutation_workflow.py::test_lane_has_an_always_run_labelled_teardown_sweep","dd_id":"focused-contracts","dd_text":"Execute the hermetic contract tests that own the edited prose."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest --collect-only -q tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/test_cloud_coordinator_lifecycle.py::test_create_and_binding_lifecycle_against_live_cloud tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/test_cloud_coordinator_lifecycle.py::test_fuse_pass_applies_a_bounded_mutation_against_live_cloud","dd_id":"live-cloud-collection","dd_text":"Collect both live cloud lifecycle nodes without executing Jira mutations."},{"command":"rtk git diff --check HEAD^ HEAD -- tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/_cloud_mutation_support.py tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/conftest.py tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/test_cloud_coordinator_lifecycle.py","dd_id":"diff-integrity","dd_text":"Reject whitespace errors in every declared path."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint && rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck","dd_id":"repository-gates","dd_text":"Run scoped lint and typecheck locally; Gerrit CI owns full-suite verification for this documentation-only leaf."}]},"source_event_uuids":["4d66635f-fea6-468c-b355-5ce103a0bb48","34ee1add-b93e-41d0-bdae-58009468deba","9b7288eb-a1be-4e38-8bf6-ddac4e85b263","e050b050-55ba-4e0e-83d8-24592373fa27","ead84711-d635-4e7b-8289-d6cc10f2f4a2","2036a04b-b3ff-418d-9ccf-647bbecd7aef","b89c8fa9-1bcb-4b8f-ba88-61afd07908a0","148e76ea-5f09-4a6c-8be0-ffd97907f457","0d112840-6fc3-4a27-a4cf-c4bc2d159845","f17c4fc0-b9b4-4952-8895-dbedcb75ba01","f91535c1-7724-49f1-a31d-98241efb5276","a953c495-f910-4e92-9f96-4b120d95f811","07a3e15c-f6a7-4c34-a672-177ede0a1098","1d628807-2337-4ec2-a38d-ec396ed4c899","633253e2-d8f1-4a17-be4c-ff4f00efb959"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788848504340434163,"uuid":"8d974792-e2f4-4a49-8e2e-bbd22ac9c68e"}